# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dedup_cleaner — weekly schedule (Monday 02:10), for the deploy box.
#
# This is a DOCUMENTATION template only. No real host names, paths, or users
# go in this file (it is committed to a public repo). Paste the concrete line
# into the deploy box's cron (user crontab or /etc/cron.d).
#
#   <deploy-user> = the unix account that runs docker on the box
#   <PROJECT_DIR> = the directory that holds docker-compose.yml + .env
#
# user crontab (`crontab -e`), 5 fields + command  :
#     10 2 * * 1  <PROJECT_DIR>/deploy/run-weekly.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
#
# /etc/cron.d/dedup-cleaner, field before command is the user:
#     10 2 * * 1  <deploy-user>  <PROJECT_DIR>/deploy/run-weekly.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
#              ^  ^^^^   ^  ^^^ ^
#           minute hour  *  *  *   Mon (0=Sun)
#
# The job is READ-ONLY (DRY_RUN stays true in the project .env). It writes a
# dated log under <PROJECT_DIR>/logs/ and keeps the 30 most recent. To review
# the latest run later, just open the newest *.log there.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
